# Fiction MCP Workflow — Walk This Way

MCPs in this workspace are **enabled** (not the June 2026 freeze). Built-in Read/Grep still win for file I/O.

## Authority order

1. `Draft_06/` prose + `PARKING_LOT.md`
2. `Story_Bible/` + `07_Pass_2_Focus.md` locks
3. Private MFA Workshop skill
4. MCP lookups — never override locked canon

## Search (period / place / facts)

Prefer in this order:

1. **Firecrawl** (`project-0-Walk This Way-firecrawl` or `user-firecrawl`) — live web, scrape, research
2. **Built-in WebSearch / WebFetch** — if Firecrawl is down or overkill
3. **Exa** — only if already authenticated; do not block a writing pass waiting on Exa login

Do not invent 1974–1979 Boston / Sudbury / WBCN facts.

## When to call which MCP

| Task | MCP |
| --- | --- |
| Character facts | `walkthisway-characters` |
| Craft / scalpel-hose | `compass-writing-guides` |
| Continuity decision | `sequential-thinking` |
| Line-edit review (when asked) | `professional-editor` |
| Style comparison | `dennis-lehane-style`, `style-emulation` |
| Scene reverse-engineering | `fiction-reverse-engineering` |
| Continuity memory | `knowledge-graph-memory` |

Skip filesystem MCP for ordinary file reads — use built-in tools.

## Before editing a chapter

1. Read the chapter file.
2. Skim `Story_Bible/07_Pass_2_Focus.md` for locks.
3. Query character MCP only when dialogue or backstory is in play.
